{
 "description": "Mean ablation where the mean is taken over a RAGGED read: the tokens of each row's entity (`{'scope': {'column': 'prompts.entity'}, 'index': ':'}` — the row's own entity text, located in its prompt — one token for Friday, three for Thursday), averaged over every entity token in the corpus, then swapped in at the answer position. A mean over a ragged read is one vector, so it lands at any window. A row whose entity text is not in its prompt is refused by name before any forward, since the data decided it; an entity that occurs twice takes its first occurrence.",
 "model": {
  "key": "hf-internal-testing/tiny-random-LlamaForCausalLM",
